{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6cd8feaa-01bd-4467-8770-e1ee140f880e","agentId":"ac00a276bc4f0d07f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are implementing Task 1: Backend project scaffold for the CLARA project.\n\n## Project Context\n\nCLARA is a policy intelligence chat app. You are building the backend — a Fastify + TypeScript API server. This is a greenfield project. The backend directory exists at `/home/advel/workplace/agora/backend/` and is empty (git repo already initialised, no code yet).\n\nThe backend will eventually expose 4 API routes (persona, chat, notes, pdf). This first task just sets up the scaffold with a health check.\n\n## Task Description\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `backend/package.json`\n- Create: `backend/tsconfig.json`\n- Create: `backend/.env.example`\n- Create: `backend/src/types.ts`\n- Create: `backend/src/index.ts`\n\n**Step 1: Initialise the backend package**\n\n```bash\ncd /home/advel/workplace/agora/backend\nnpm init -y\nnpm install fastify @fastify/cors @fastify/multipart @anthropic-ai/sdk pdf-parse dotenv\nnpm install --save-dev typescript @types/node vitest tsx @types/pdf-parse\n```\n\nExpected: `node_modules/` created, no errors.\n\n**Step 2: Write `backend/tsconfig.json`**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"module\": \"CommonJS\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Node\",\n    \"outDir\": \"./dist\",\n    \"rootDir\": \"./src\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src\", \"tests\"]\n}\n```\n\n**Step 3: Write `backend/.env.example`**\n\n```\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here\nPORT=3000\n```\n\nCopy to `.env`:\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\n```\n(Leave the placeholder value — no real key needed for this task)\n\n**Step 4: Write `backend/src/types.ts`**\n\n```typescript\nexport interface ProfileAnswers {\n  name: string\n  situation: string\n  city: string\n  concern: string\n  language: string\n}\n\nexport interface Message {\n  role: 'user' | 'assistant'\n  content: string\n}\n\nexport interface NoteGroup {\n  title: string\n  items: string[]\n}\n\nexport interface PolicyResult {\n  title: string\n  summary: string\n  source: string\n  relevanceScore: number\n}\n```\n\n**Step 5: Write `backend/src/index.ts`**\n\n```typescript\nimport 'dotenv/config'\nimport Fastify from 'fastify'\nimport cors from '@fastify/cors'\n\nconst app = Fastify({ logger: true })\n\nasync function start() {\n  await app.register(cors, {\n    origin: ['http://localhost:5173', 'http://frontend:5173'],\n  })\n\n  app.get('/health', async () => ({ status: 'ok' }))\n\n  const port = Number(process.env.PORT) || 3000\n  await app.listen({ port, host: '0.0.0.0' })\n}\n\nstart().catch(console.error)\n```\n\n**Step 6: Add scripts to `backend/package.json`**\n\nMerge these scripts into package.json (do NOT add `\"type\": \"module\"` — the backend uses CommonJS):\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\",\n    \"build\": \"tsc\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Step 7: Verify the server starts**\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nExpected output includes: `Server listening at http://0.0.0.0:3000`\n\nIn a second terminal (or use curl in background):\n```bash\ncurl http://localhost:3000/health\n```\n\nExpected: `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`\n\nKill the dev server after verifying.\n\n**Step 8: Commit**\n\n```bash\ncd /home/advel/workplace/agora/backend\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat: scaffold backend with Fastify and health check\"\n```\n\n## Notes\n- Work directory: `/home/advel/workplace/agora/backend`\n- Use CommonJS (no `\"type\": \"module\"` in package.json)\n- The `.env` file with placeholder value is OK to commit for now — the real key will be added by the team\n\n## Report Format\n\nWhen done:\n- **Status:** DONE | DONE_WITH_CONCERNS | BLOCKED | NEEDS_CONTEXT\n- What you implemented\n- Test results\n- Files changed\n- Any concerns\n"},"uuid":"113e02e5-e8